view formula-cost-value-return | cost-price-value-return | dollar-return,rate-of-return,present-value | formula | Cost, Value, and Return Relations | tables/formulas/cost-value-return.md | These relations calculate one holding-period return and single-cash-flow present/future value. They do not define all cost, price, value, utility, or investment decisions. Cash-flow boundary, dates, rate basis, periods, compounding, currency basis, and risk assumptions remain mandatory.
end-view
view formula-density | matter-load-measure | mass-density | formula | Mass Density | tables/formulas/density.md | Average mass density relates the total mass of a chosen object or substance sample to the volume it occupies. The bulk relation does not by itself assert that density is uniform at every point.
end-view
view formula-electrical-quantities | electrical-quantity | electric-charge,electric-current,potential-difference,electrical-power,electrical-energy-transfer | formula | Electrical Quantities | tables/formulas/electrical-quantities.md | These relations separate charge, current, potential difference, electrical power, and transferred energy. They require a system or component, terminal pair or oriented surface, time basis, and consistent voltage-current sign convention.
end-view
view formula-force | force | physical-interaction | formula | Force - Newtonian Net-Force Formula View | tables/formulas/force.md | In Newtonian mechanics, Newton's second law relates the net external force on a chosen system to its mass and acceleration. The familiar `F = ma` shorthand is useful only when `F` is understood as the vector sum of external forces and the system and model assumptions are fixed.
end-view
view formula-general-accounting-balance | stock-flow-balance | stock,flow,accumulation,balance,conservation | formula | General Accounting Balance | tables/formulas/general-accounting-balance.md | An accounting balance tracks a countable property inside a chosen system over time. Input and generation add to the system; output and consumption remove from it. When the property is strictly conserved, generation and consumption are zero.
end-view
view formula-information-signal-measures | information-data-signal-noise | self-information,shannon-entropy,signal-to-noise-ratio | formula | Information and Signal Measures | tables/formulas/information-signal-measures.md | These relations quantify modeled surprise, average discrete uncertainty, and selected signal-to-noise comparisons. They do not measure semantic meaning, truth, usefulness, or universal signal quality.
end-view
view formula-kinematics-motion-measures | motion-measure | position,distance-traveled,displacement,speed,velocity,acceleration | formula | Kinematics Motion Measures | tables/formulas/kinematics-motion-measures.md | These relations separate path-based scalars from endpoint- or derivative-based vectors. Average relations use finite intervals; instantaneous relations use derivatives. Constant-acceleration equations form a narrower conditional view.
end-view
view formula-matter-load-measures | matter-load-measure | mass,weight,mass-density,pressure | formula | Matter and Load Measures | tables/formulas/matter-load-measures.md | These relations distinguish a base quantity from gravitational force and from volume- or area-normalized quantities. Their short algebra is useful only when the subject boundary, environment, averaging scope, and loaded geometry are known.
end-view
view formula-mechanical-work-energy-power | work-energy-power | mechanical-work,energy,kinetic-energy,potential-energy,power | formula | Mechanical Work, Energy, and Power | tables/formulas/mechanical-work-energy-power.md | These relations connect force-displacement transfer, mechanical-energy state terms, and transfer rate. They require an explicit system, path, frame, potential reference, and model scope.
end-view
view formula-newtons-method | mathematical-relation-solving | mathematical-function,root,derivative,iteration,convergence | formula | Newton's Method | tables/formulas/newtons-method.md | Newton's method iteratively approximates a root of a differentiable function by intersecting the tangent at the current estimate with the horizontal axis. Its familiar fast convergence is local and conditional, not guaranteed from every starting value.
end-view
view formula-ohms-law | electrical-quantity | electric-current,potential-difference,resistance | formula | Ohm's Law | tables/formulas/ohms-law.md | Ohm's law describes a linear voltage-current relation for an ohmic material or component under the physical conditions for which its resistance remains applicable. Despite its familiar name, it is an empirical relation rather than a universal law of nature.
end-view
view formula-periodic-wave-quantities | periodic-wave-quantity | period,frequency,angular-frequency,wavelength,wave-number,phase,wave-speed,oscillation,amplitude,spectrum,phase-velocity,group-velocity | formula | Periodic and Wave Quantities | tables/formulas/periodic-wave-quantities.md | These relations connect recurrence, sinusoidal representation, a finite discrete transform, component phase speed, and local group velocity. Reference, sampling, normalization, propagation sign, medium, mode, dispersion branch, bandwidth, and validity regime remain part of the formula contract.
end-view
view formula-probability-range | probability-risk-uncertainty | event-probability | formula | Event Probability Range | tables/formulas/probability-range.md | Within a probability model, every event receives a probability between zero and one inclusive. The bound is a mathematical constraint on a probability measure; it does not make every arbitrary score in that interval a calibrated probability.
end-view
view formula-probability-risk-uncertainty | probability-risk-uncertainty | event-probability,conditional-probability,odds-in-favor,risk,expected-loss,uncertainty,measurement-uncertainty | formula | Probability, Risk, and Uncertainty Relations | tables/formulas/probability-risk-uncertainty.md | These relations connect event probability, odds, consequence-valued expectation, and measurement uncertainty. Risk itself remains a declared model family rather than one universal multiplication rule.
end-view
view formula-pythagorean-trigonometric-identity | mathematical-relation-solving | identity,equation | formula | Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity | tables/formulas/pythagorean-trigonometric-identity.md | The Pythagorean trigonometric identity states a relation that holds for every real angle under the standard sine and cosine definitions. It is an identity, not an empirical law and not an equation that selects particular solutions.
end-view
view formula-thermal-quantities | thermal-quantity | temperature,thermal-equilibrium,heat-transfer,internal-energy,heat-capacity,specific-heat-capacity,entropy | formula | Thermal Quantities | tables/formulas/thermal-quantities.md | These relations separate thermal state variables from path-dependent heat and work transfers. They require a system boundary, process conditions, sign convention, phase scope, and absolute temperature where entropy is involved.
end-view
view mapping-factor-role-mechanisms | factorization-quality | mechanism-assignment | mapping | Factor Role to Mechanism Crosswalk | tables/mappings/factor-role-mechanisms.md | Maps eleven general factor roles into six bounded target-system mechanism vocabularies while preserving contextual, partial, many-to-many semantics and explicit non-equivalence.
end-view
view mapping-governance-compliance-mechanisms | governance-obligation-compliance | governance,obligation,compliance | mapping | Governance and Compliance Mechanisms | tables/mappings/governance-compliance-mechanisms.md | Maps governance, obligation, and compliance concepts to bounded organizational records, compliance systems, policies, controls, enforcement points, assessments, and attestations while preserving authority, applicability, evidence, effectiveness, and non-equivalence.
end-view
view mapping-organizational-assignment-semantics | organization-role-authority | organization,organizational-role,responsibility,authority,accountability-answerability,action-accountability,delegation,ownership-stewardship | mapping | Organizational Assignment Semantics | tables/mappings/organizational-assignment-semantics.md | Maps canonical organization, role, responsibility, authority, accountability, delegation, and stewardship concepts to common organizational records while preserving contextual, partial, many-to-many semantics and explicit non-equivalence.
end-view
view mapping-software-architecture-mechanisms | software-module-service-resource | module,service,resource | mapping | Software Architecture Mechanisms | tables/mappings/software-architecture-mechanisms.md | Maps module, service, and resource concepts into bounded language, SOA, HTTP, and Kubernetes mechanisms while preserving namespace, capability-access, resource, representation, state, lifecycle, and non-equivalence distinctions.
end-view
view mapping-software-interaction-mechanisms | software-transaction-message-contract | transaction,message,contract | mapping | Software Interaction Mechanisms | tables/mappings/software-interaction-mechanisms.md | Maps transaction, message, and contract concepts into bounded database, HTTP, SOA, API-description, and assertion mechanisms while separating acknowledgment, commit, business completion, event, representation, schema, and behavioral obligations.
end-view
view mapping-software-program-constructs | software-type-value-function | type,value,function | mapping | Software Program Construct Mechanisms | tables/mappings/software-program-constructs.md | Maps type, value, and function concepts into bounded Rust, Haskell, and PostgreSQL mechanisms without treating classes, variables, representations, signatures, purity, or target syntax as universal definitions.
end-view
view mapping-temperature-scales | thermal-quantity | temperature | mapping | Temperature Scale Conversion | tables/mappings/temperature-scales.md | Celsius, kelvin, and Fahrenheit assign different numerical values to the same point temperature. Point-temperature conversion is affine because scale and zero point may differ. Temperature intervals use scale only and MUST NOT reuse the point offset.
end-view
view mapping-version-scheme-semantics | identity-naming-classification-versioning | version,compatibility-level | mapping | Version Scheme Semantics | tables/mappings/version-scheme-semantics.md | Generic version roles map to Semantic Versioning only when a package declares a public API.
end-view
view procedure-entry-publication | factorium-entry-publication | editorial-workflow,entry-maturity,publication-state,source-authority,domain-acceptance | procedure | Entry Publication Procedure | tables/procedures/entry-publication.md | Research, canonicalization, specialized views, role review, validation, integration, and publication use explicit gates and recovery.
end-view
view reference-value-si-defining-constants | physical-constant | defining-constant | reference-value | SI Defining Constants | tables/values/si-defining-constants.md | Exact SI defining values retain their quantities, symbols, units, defining status, authority, and scope.
end-view
view scale-editorial-maturity | factorium-entry-publication | entry-maturity | scale | Editorial Maturity Scale | tables/scales/editorial-maturity.md | Candidate, supported, established, disputed, and deprecated are evidence-backed interpretations rather than automatic scores.
end-view
view transition-generic-lifecycle | state-event-transition-process-lifecycle | transition,lifecycle-stage,status | transition | Generic Lifecycle Transition Table | tables/transitions/generic-lifecycle.md | A lifecycle change preserves source, event, guard, effect, target, and failure behavior as distinct fields.
end-view
end-reference
